  "result": "`python3 -m shop quote a:12.5:2` now prints 27.06. All 6 tests pass.\n\n**Root cause:** `to_cents` in `shop/money.py` padded a one-digit fraction on the left. `\"12.5\"` became 12 dollars and `\"05\"` cents, so it was read as 1205 cents instead of 1250. The quote used a price of 12.05, which gives 24.10 plus 1.99 tax, or 26.09.\n\n**Fix:** I changed `frac.rjust(2, \"0\")` to `frac.ljust(2, \"0\")`, so `\"5\"` becomes `\"50\"`. With the fix, 2 \u00d7 12.50 = 25.00, plus 8.25% tax (2.06 after rounding), gives 27.06.\n\nNo existing test covers one-digit decimals like `12.5`, which is why the tests didn't catch this. I didn't add one.",
